%% DESIGNED, nothing built (docs/architecture/registry-gate.md, "Status, 2026-10-20: a design for review"). Open there: where the PKI lives, a push by a Polar account
%% (c:push-image), a new crate, the gate's own image pinned by digest. Today the registry in the cluster has no authentication (infra/cluster-registry.nu).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Up as up.nu<br/>(the registry step)
    participant PKI as The deployment's PKI
    participant Node as A node (kubelet)
    actor Op as Operator (pusher)
    participant Gate as The gate
    participant Reg as The upstream registry<br/>(127.0.0.1:5000 only)
    participant Log as Append-only log
    participant Cassini

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Up,Cassini: DESIGNED: the gate is the only way in
    Up->>PKI: make the server certificate and the pusher's client certificate, if absent

    Node->>Gate: pull: plain HTTP, by the NodePort, GET or HEAD under /v2/
    Gate->>Reg: passed through
    Gate-->>Node: any other method is refused

    Op->>Gate: push: mTLS, by the ClusterIP through a port-forward, as pusher
    Gate->>Gate: the exact identity. DELETE is refused to everyone
    Gate->>Reg: passed through
    loop each manifest
        Gate->>Log: who, digest, tag, address
        Gate-)Cassini: an event, once Cassini runs
    end
    end
